# Visual Studio / .NET — standard ignores for Winmega (WinUI 3)
# The template shipped only ".vs/", which let obj/ build output and
# Omega.csproj.user get committed. Never track build output or user files.

## VS / user-specific
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## Build output
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Ww][Ii][Nn]32/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/
bld/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

## NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
**/[Pp]ackages/*
!**/[Pp]ackages/build/
*.nuget.props
*.nuget.targets
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

## MSIX / packaging output
AppPackages/
BundleArtifacts/
*.msix
*.msixupload
*.appx
*.appxupload
*.appxbundle
*.msixbundle
# Signing material — NEVER commit certificates or passwords
*.pfx
*.p12
*.cer

